# LCB Training Web — agent workflow

Work in `lcb-training-web/` unless the task says otherwise.

## After any code change

Before telling the user the task is done:

1. Run `npm run check:ascii` from `lcb-training-web/` (valid UTF-8 + ASCII-only in scanned source).
2. Run `npm run typecheck`.
3. Fix any errors; re-run until both pass.
4. Do not claim completion if either step failed or was skipped.

Source under `app/`, `lib/`, `components/`, `scripts/`, and `content/` must be ASCII-only UTF-8: straight quotes and apostrophes, `-` not em/en dashes, `...` not ellipsis. Do not paste smart punctuation from user copy into code.

`npm run dev` runs `predev` (`check:ascii`) automatically. `next dev` does not replace typecheck; API routes and server code must pass `tsc --noEmit`.

## Before any push

Run the full gate from `lcb-training-web/` in order:

1. `npm run check:ascii`
2. `npm run typecheck`
3. Every `test:*` script in `package.json` (all must pass):

```bash
npm run test:program-schedule && \
npm run test:program-send-windows && \
npm run test:daily-plan && \
npm run test:strength-extra-work && \
npm run test:quiz && \
npm run test:coach-daily-summary-business && \
npm run test:program-stats && \
npm run test:program-task-completion && \
npm run test:coaching-submissions && \
npm run test:written-report-parse && \
npm run test:written-report-line && \
npm run test:player-evaluation-pdf && \
npm run test:player-evaluation-cta && \
npm run test:reports-queue && \
npm run test:admin-sent-reports && \
npm run test:coaching-submission-confirmation && \
npm run test:playbook-entitlements && \
npm run test:access && \
npm run test:org-weekly-focus && \
npm run test:drill-focus-grants && \
npm run test:org-trial-dashboard && \
npm run test:resources && \
npm run test:resource-download-gate && \
npm run test:fix-it-plans && \
npm run test:video-poster-capture && \
npm run test:my-resources && \
npm run test:dev-environment-guard && \
npm run test:subscriptions
```

4. `npm run build` (production build; includes `check:ascii` and `prisma generate`).

Only push when the user explicitly asks. Never push if any step failed.

## Local Stripe + dev server

When (re)starting local setup or after the user asks:

1. Stop existing `stripe listen` and `next dev` if needed.
2. Start Stripe CLI (from `lcb-training-web/`):

```bash
stripe listen \
  --events checkout.session.completed,customer.subscription.created,customer.subscription.updated,customer.subscription.deleted,invoice.paid,invoice.payment_failed,charge.refunded \
  --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhooks/stripe
```

Do not use `--all-thin`.

3. Copy the CLI `whsec_...` into `.env` as `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` if it changed; restart dev if `.env` was updated.
4. Run `npm run dev` in a separate process.
5. Confirm both are ready, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` matches the running `stripe listen` secret, and `http://localhost:3000` returns 200 without compile errors.

See `docs/STRIPE_LOCAL_WEBHOOKS.md` and `docs/DEV_SETUP.md` for details.

## Database migrations (local / dev)

Apply schema migrations only via:

```bash
npm run db:migrate:dev
```

(from `lcb-training-web/`, with dev `.env` loaded). Do **not** run `npx prisma migrate deploy` or `npm run prisma:deploy` directly in agent workflows; use the npm script so the same guardrails and docs apply. Never migrate against production unless the user explicitly requests production ops.
